- An issued certificate carries an authority key identifier, which names the key that signed
- it. That is how a verifier finds the root in a chain. An
- [HTTP server](http-server.md) presents such a certificate over TLS.
+ Un certificado emitido lleva un identificador de clave de la autoridad, que nombra la clave
+ que lo firmó. Así es como un verificador encuentra la raíz en una cadena. Un
+ [servidor HTTP](http-server.md) presenta un certificado así sobre TLS.

- ### Keystores
+ ### Almacenes de claves

- A [PKCS#12](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/PKCS_12) keystore is opened for the duration of a
- scope. The password is given as an opaque `Password`, so its cleartext is reached only
- through the scoped `Cleartext` capability, and the character array which the platform needs
- is zeroed once the store is loaded. Inside the scope, `keystore` is the open store:
+ Un almacén de claves [PKCS#12](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/PKCS_12) se abre durante un
+ ámbito. La contraseña se da como una `Password` opaca, así que su texto en claro solo se
+ alcanza mediante la capacidad `Cleartext` del ámbito, y el array de caracteres que necesita la
+ plataforma se pone a cero en cuanto se carga el almacén. Dentro del ámbito, `keystore` es el
+ almacén abierto:

= is zeroed once the store is loaded. Inside the scope, `keystore` is the open store:
=
- ```scala
+ ```scala

- import pathInterfaces.pathOnLinux
+ import pathInterfaces.pathOnLinux

- import temporaryDirectories.javaBaseTemporaryDirectory
+ import temporaryDirectories.javaBaseTemporaryDirectory

- val storePath = temporaryDirectory[Path on Linux] / "cryptography" / "store.p12"
+ val storePath = temporaryDirectory[Path on Linux] / "cryptography" / "store.p12"

- def readAliases(): List[Text] =
+ def readAliases(): List[Text] =

-   storePath.open[Keystore](Password(t"sesame")):
+   storePath.open[Keystore](Password(t"sesame")):

-     val server = keystore.certificate(t"server")
+     val server = keystore.certificate(t"server")

-     keystore.aliases
+     keystore.aliases

=     keystore.aliases
- ```
+ ```

- An alias which the store does not hold gives `Unset`. A wrong password and a corrupt store
- are deliberately indistinguishable: both are `Unreadable` in the `Keystore.Error`. Telling
- them apart would tell someone who was guessing which of the two had gone wrong.
+ Un alias que el almacén no contiene da `Unset`. Una contraseña equivocada y un almacén
+ corrupto son indistinguibles a propósito: ambos son `Unreadable` en el `Keystore.Error`.
+ Distinguirlos le diría a quien estuviera adivinando cuál de los dos ha fallado.

- ### Weak algorithms
+ ### Algoritmos débiles

- Encrypting with DES, RC2, 1024-bit RSA, ECB mode, or any unauthenticated block cipher, needs a
- permission from the package `cryptoPermits` in scope. These are the same
- [permits](hashing.md#weak-algorithms) which gate MD5 and SHA-1. Accepting legacy cryptography
- is thus an explicit decision which can be audited, not a default. The permits nest, and
- `permitDisallowedCrypto` includes every other:
+ Cifrar con DES, RC2, RSA de 1024 bits, el modo ECB o cualquier cifrado por bloques sin
+ autenticación necesita en el ámbito un permiso del paquete `cryptoPermits`. Son los mismos
+ [permisos](hashing.md#weak-algorithms) que protegen MD5 y SHA-1. Aceptar la criptografía
+ heredada es así una decisión explícita que puede auditarse, no un comportamiento por defecto.
+ Los permisos se anidan, y `permitDisallowedCrypto` incluye todos los demás:

= `permitDisallowedCrypto` includes every other:
=
- ```tabular
+ ```tabular

- column  Algorithm
- column  Permitted by
- row  any block cipher, which is unauthenticated  `permitUnauthenticatedCrypto`
- row  Triple-DES  `permitDeprecatedCrypto`; to decrypt or verify only, `permitLegacyCrypto`
- row  DSA  `permitDisallowedCrypto`; to verify only, `permitLegacyCrypto`
+ column  Algoritmo
+ column  Lo permite
+ row  cualquier cifrado por bloques, que no está autenticado  `permitUnauthenticatedCrypto`
+ row  Triple-DES  `permitDeprecatedCrypto`; solo para descifrar o verificar, `permitLegacyCrypto`
+ row  DSA  `permitDisallowedCrypto`; solo para verificar, `permitLegacyCrypto`

- row  DES, RC2, Blowfish  `permitDisallowedCrypto`
+ row  DES, RC2, Blowfish  `permitDisallowedCrypto`

- row  1024-bit RSA  `permitDisallowedCrypto`
- row  ECB mode  `permitDisallowedCrypto`
+ row  RSA de 1024 bits  `permitDisallowedCrypto`
+ row  Modo ECB  `permitDisallowedCrypto`

= row  ECB mode  `permitDisallowedCrypto`
- ```
+ ```

- Across the algorithms, these are the operations which each supports, and the permit it needs:
+ En el conjunto de los algoritmos, estas son las operaciones que admite cada uno, y el permiso
+ que necesita:

= Across the algorithms, these are the operations which each supports, and the permit it needs:
=
- ```tabular
+ ```tabular

- column  Algorithm
- column  Operations
- column  Permit
- row  `Aes[128 | 192 | 256]`  encrypt, decrypt  `permitUnauthenticatedCrypto`
- row  `TripleDes[112 | 168]`  encrypt, decrypt  `permitDeprecatedCrypto`
